# `+` and `*` on a figure no verified invariant bounds: exact when it fits,
# checkable against `core` (overflow checks on or off).
fig_add	core library	Kani	discharged (Kani: kani_proofs::stats::fig_add_exact)
fig_add64	core library	Kani	discharged (Kani: kani_proofs::stats::fig_add64_exact)
fig_mul	core library	Kani	discharged (Kani: kani_proofs::stats::fig_mul_exact)
# A lock's invariant: its writer `Shared::init` (`Snapshot::EMPTY`) is
# not verified yet; `collect_into` asserts it.
axiom_snapshot_lock_inv	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# The scratch pool hands each object to one call at a time (a slot's
# holder thread ID, taken by compare-exchange, or the thread's own when its
# holding frame is gone by the stack mark), the residue of a call from an
# alternate stack or context above the holder's aside (two calls collect
# into one object: wrong figures, no freed memory); pooled objects are
# never freed. A release frees the mark before the owner, and a take moves
# the mark by compare-exchange, so a call that a handler on its stack
# interrupted between reading a slot and taking it does not take the slot
# the handler used and gave back. A `fork` from inside a statistics
# callback: the child's fork handler re-owns the forking thread's slots
# under its new thread ID (pool_fork_prepare records the old one), so the
# child's copy of the call keeps its object.
pool_take	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
pool_reserve	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
pool_fill	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
pool_unreserve	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
pool_release	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
pool_fork_prepare	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
pool_fork_child	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# Temporary seam, provable in Verus once the snapshot lock's frame is
# stated, which its explicit `g.unlock()` requires.
collect_into	allocator invariant	Verus
